<title>UK: Grand Met/Guinness merger will cut 2,000 jobs.</title>
<headline>Grand Met/Guinness merger will cut 2,000 jobs.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The planned merger between Britain's brewing and spiritis giants' Grand Metropolitan plc and Guinness plc will result in the loss of 2,000 jobs in the spirits business, the group chief executive of the new company said.  </p>
<p>&quot;There will be approximately 2,000 job losses out of 20,000 people in the spirits business,&quot; said John McGrath, who is group chief executive of CMG Brands, the world's seventh largest food and drinks company created by the merger.</p>
<p>McGrath said the job cuts will be dispersed throughout the new company's global operations. The companies have a combined workforce of 85,000.</p>
<p>&quot;There will be no pockets,&quot; he said.</p>
</text>
